  1132	The split between local references and portable values follows
  1133	`yin.vm.macro.md` §4.1 exactly (`yin.vm.macro.md:692-708`), and it is
  1134	enforced by how the transactor resolves ids: `apply-tempid-map` replaces a
  1135	tempid in `v` **only when the whole value is a tempid on a declared
  1136	reference attribute** (`src/cljc/dao/space/transact.cljc:168-185`); a
  1137	tempid nested inside a vector is left as it is. Therefore:
  1138	
  1139	- an **initial** expansion's call sits in admitted syntax, so it carries
  1140	  `:yin.ledger/origin`, a value `[:source medium batch j]` including the
  1141	  batch member index: the successor of `:yin/source-call` qualified by
  1142	  `:yin/source-batch`, which no transactor resolves, as today;
  1143	- a **nested** expansion's call sits in the output of the enclosing
  1144	  expansion, so it carries **two** links to the parent: `:yin.ledger/
  1145	  parent-event`, a declared reference attribute whose whole value is the
  1146	  parent event's id, the successor of `:yin/source-node` and resolved by
  1147	  the transactor within the log medium exactly as `:yin/source-node` is
  1148	  today; and `:yin.ledger/parent`, the parent's **record address**, which
  1149	  is a value and travels. The parent is complete before the child begins,
  1150	  because a nested expansion's input is the enclosing expansion's output
  1151	  (`yin.vm.macro.md:698-701`), so the parent's record address is known
  1152	  when the child's record is minted; no staging after allocation is
  1153	  needed, and the record (§8.2) never contains a log-local id, so it is
  1154	  hashed once, when built.
  1155	
