   267	   `k` and that `:name` matches); it can therefore move a harvested
   268	   declaration's effective position — re-asserting it after a plain
   269	   definition, say — but never introduce an unharvested body. That is
   270	   permitted transformer behaviour and is stated as such. Stand-ins resolve
   271	   exclusively against the *current* batch's fresh catalogue and carry no
   272	   cross-batch declaration identity; marker-shaped data may well survive
   273	   outside one expansion (it is plain data), and if replayed it selects
